Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-83: outline keys, Navigate to Event Handler from
 the HTML, the form shown first -- like WPF (0.83.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "你看還有那邊跟wpf不一樣 直接做修改 你每次修改需要自己做記錄".
The record is WPF_DIFF_LOG.md (new): what WPF does (Microsoft's pages), what
this did, what it does now, the test, the version; the open ones on top.
- the Document Outline's keys (WPF: the outline does what the design surface
  does): F2 rename, Ctrl+C / X / V, Delete bound in the component tree
  (outlineKey) -- on the tree's selected row, which the arrow keys move without
  the page knowing, so it is selected first (several rows: the page has them).
- 移到事件處理函式 in the page's HTML (WPF: right-click the event in XAML ->
  "Navigate to Event Handler"): on a designer event's htdCpp(...) line = that
  C++ function (the open not-saved .cpp too); anywhere else in an element = its
  default event's code, as F7 (nothing added). The HTML's right-click also has
  檢視設計工具 (Shift+F7).
- nothing picked yet = the form is the selection (WPF: the Properties window
  shows the Window): the first init without selectId selects the form (only
  when nothing is selected).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 169, panels, real VS Code 149): probe
(a first init selects @form), smoke (Ctrl+C on the tree's Panel2 row copies
Panel2 while the page had spbSave; the five keys bound; the htdCpp line ->
TfHotPlate::spbSaveUp), real VS Code (the cursor in spbSave -> its OnClick's
C++ opens, nothing changed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
